{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.GreedyLadderTermination","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.GreedyLadderTermination","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.exists_rung_hitting_target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.exists_rung_hitting_target","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GreedyLadderTermination.lean#L82-L90","doc":"**The one-rung model is an exact interpolant, not an approximation.**\n\nStated without reference to the extraction: for any `Qbase` and any nonzero\nscale, there is a coefficient making the model hit the target exactly. So\n\"the ladder reproduces CODATA\" is a property of having one free coefficient,\ncarrying no information about the model that coefficient multiplies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.greedy_later_rungs_vanish","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.greedy_later_rungs_vanish","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GreedyLadderTermination.lean#L71-L80","doc":"**Any further extracted rung is zero.**\n\nWhatever scale `y` a later rung is extracted at, its coefficient is the\nresidual over `y`, and the residual is zero — so every rung beyond the first\nextracted one vanishes identically. `c_4 … c_7` carry no information; they are\nnot small, they are `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.greedy_next_residual_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.greedy_next_residual_zero","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GreedyLadderTermination.lean#L61-L69","doc":"**The residual after the extracted rung is exactly zero.**\n\nConsequently the producer's `abs(ratio_m1) < EPS_RESIDUAL` guard fires at the\nvery next `k`, whatever `EPS_RESIDUAL` is — the ladder stops after one\nextracted rung, not because it converged but because it was solved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.greedy_rung_exact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.greedy_rung_exact","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GreedyLadderTermination.lean#L47-L59","doc":"**The extracted rung reproduces the target exactly.**\n\n`rung` is the coefficient the producer extracts at scale `x` (there `x = uᵏ`):\nit is *defined* as the relative shortfall divided by `x`. Applying it to\n`Qprev` therefore lands on `Qtarget` identically, for every nonzero `Qprev`\nand `x`.\n\nThis is the algebraic content of the runtime line\n`c_4: residual below compute precision (0.00e+00)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}